# Hub room

Your room is the seat entry with `runtime: "cursor"` in `.agents/SYSTEM/hub-partner-seats.json` whose key is this worktree's seat (`sia-<seat>`). The `talk` line there is the invocation. Substitute `{hub_url}`, `{hub_name}` and `{room}` from `dispatch.cursor.room` on that seat. There is no top-level `room`. `ob_start` reads the same file's `readers` map.

If your seat row has `runtime: "cursor"`, your waker starts this chat when atlas posts a turn. At the start of the run, run the `talk` line with `--inbox` before other work.

An unread atlas turn is the assignment. Do not propose a backlog item beside it.

Do the work, then post your reply with `--say`. When the post succeeds, end this turn. Never block on hub-talk waiting for the next atlas turn in this run — the waker starts the next run when that turn arrives. Post when the work is done, not a bare acknowledgement.

When you run hub-talk with `--inbox` or `--say`, act on the exit code (A2A-Hub Loop 13, master 8e59f58, `docs/loops/loop-13-design-ruling.md`): exit 0, a turn was printed, act on it (the atlas turn, in this same turn for `--inbox`). Exit 1, refused or called wrong: fix the call and do not retry. Exit 2, the window elapsed: wait again. Exit 3, unavailable or throttled: the last stderr line is `[hub-talk] retry status=<code|network> retry-after=<seconds|unknown>`; wait `retry-after` seconds, otherwise back off 5 s doubling to 60 s; after 5 consecutive exit-3 results over 2 minutes with no `retry-after`, stop and report.

Start every work reply, in the hub and in chat, with one line `TASK: <task id> <phase>, <what> (<branch>)`, and update it as the work changes. The dashboard reads a Cursor seat's current dispatch only from that line, because it does not parse hub-talk output (T-235).

Turn-end and wait: A2A-Hub master b6a8de79 (PR 250), `.agents/roles/shared.md` § Hub transport: how a seat waits (T-103, revised 2026-10-05) — a Cursor seat with a waker never waits inside its turn; only a seat with no waker waits in the foreground. D-120: keep working until the assignment is FROZEN or BLOCKED before you post; ending the turn after you post is not permission to stop mid-work. Native A2A is Claude-to-Claude only; this hub carries the Cursor seats.
